    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Description\n\nI feel like it would be quite useful to have a little preview of the scope borders for the cases when the border is outside the current view of the window.\n\nThis would be especially useful when `indent_at_cursor` is set and there are multiple indentation scopes outside the view (Example: A function, a try statement, an if statement are all declared higher up in the file. Moving the cursor horizontally displays the function declaration, the try block start and the if statement).\n\nWhile this mostly makes sense for the top border, the bottom border can also be useful for cases like `else if` or the `while` in a `do-while` expression.\n\nWhat I came up with looks like this:\n\nCode:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53ffcd6f-b21c-4cb5-95ee-76e7f07ad0b4)\n\nPreview:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/25dfe39a-a5d0-4214-bc86-a4a351bdc2ef)\n\nThe idea would be to further improve this using treesitter to show the whole header of the border node (e.g. all lines of a multi-line function signature)\n\nThanks in advance for the feedback :)",
