            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nMy first instinct is that this functionality (especially the tree-sitter part) doesn't quite fit 'mini.indentscope' design. It would require pretty big chunk of a new code without much of justification for it to specifically be a part of 'mini.indentscope'.\n\nThis looks like a better fit for #983, a more general version of which (something like 'mini.hierarchy') *is* planned. For some ideas see bottom part of [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1780#issuecomment-2850337535).\n\nI'll ponder a bit on this idea, though.",
